From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Skip an async I/O status block seen to be unwritable.

When an asynchronous I/O completes, invoke_system_apc() handles the
APC_ASYNC_IO system APC and set_async_iosb() writes the result to the
caller's IO status block. The server delivers a system APC to a thread
that is not waiting for one with SIGUSR1, so the write can run on the
signal stack. handle_syscall_fault() does not cover the signal stack, so
if the block is no longer writable the fault ends in
virtual_setup_exception() as a nested exception and the thread is
aborted, together with any lock it holds.

This was reproduced on the first Steam start in a fresh prefix: after
the 32-bit bootstrapper had committed its update, it faulted in
invoke_system_apc() writing the Information field of a WoW64 status
block, was aborted holding the loader lock, and the process hung. Why
the block was no longer writable is not known.

Before the write, read the protection of every page of the block and
skip the write, logging it once per process, when a page is seen to be
uncommitted, guarded or not writable; memory that Wine does not track
counts as uncommitted. Otherwise write it with the existing
set_async_iosb(), so the status is still stored last with release
semantics. Write-watched pages count as writable and go through the
existing write fault path. The result returned to the server, and so
the event, APC and completion port notification, is unchanged.

This also changes the completion that runs inside a wait: there the
fault used to be returned by handle_syscall_fault(), so the wait failed
with STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION (a guard page was cleared and reported as a
guard page violation) and the I/O never completed. Now the write is
skipped and the I/O completes.

This is a limited guard, not a safe write. The protection table is read
without the virtual lock: the interrupted thread may hold host locks,
such as the dyld lock, that a virtual lock owner can be waiting for in
dlopen(). The pages can therefore still be released, decommitted or
reprotected before or while the block is written, and that write faults
as before. The completion path as a whole still takes the virtual lock
on write-watch faults and in some I/O callbacks. A guard page is skipped
and left armed; that, like ignoring the failed write at all, has not
been measured on Windows. ReactOS ignores a failed status block write
when completing an IRP.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index 1e77a4e..fc0196b 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -417,7 +417,14 @@ static void invoke_system_apc( const union apc_call *call, union apc_result *res
             result->async_io.status = status;
             result->async_io.total = info;
             /* the server will pass us NULL if a call failed synchronously */
-            set_async_iosb( call->async_io.sb, result->async_io.status, info );
+            if (!virtual_set_async_iosb( call->async_io.sb, result->async_io.status, info ))
+            {
+                /* the I/O still completes; only the status block write is skipped */
+                static LONG reported;
+                if (!InterlockedExchange( &reported, 1 ))
+                    ERR( "skipping unwritable async I/O status block %s, I/O status %#x\n",
+                         wine_dbgstr_longlong( call->async_io.sb ), result->async_io.status );
+            }
         }
         else result->async_io.status = STATUS_PENDING; /* restart it */
         break;
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h b/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
index 269e376..3a81a34 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/unix_private.h
@@ -313,6 +313,7 @@ extern BOOL virtual_check_buffer_for_read( const void *ptr, SIZE_T size );
 extern BOOL virtual_check_buffer_for_write( void *ptr, SIZE_T size );
 extern SIZE_T virtual_uninterrupted_read_memory( const void *addr, void *buffer, SIZE_T size );
 extern NTSTATUS virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( void *addr, const void *buffer, SIZE_T size );
+extern BOOL virtual_set_async_iosb( client_ptr_t iosb, NTSTATUS status, ULONG_PTR info );
 extern void virtual_set_force_exec( BOOL enable );
 extern void virtual_enable_write_exceptions( BOOL enable );
 extern void virtual_init_rosetta_smc_step(void);
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index a61e5bd..a6b9af7 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5057,6 +5057,40 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_uninterrupted_write_memory( void *addr, const void *buffer, SIZ
 }
 
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           virtual_set_async_iosb
+ *
+ * Store the result of a completed asynchronous I/O in its IO status block
+ * with set_async_iosb(), unless a page of the block is seen to be uncommitted,
+ * guarded or not writable. The completion runs in a system APC, which may be
+ * invoked on the signal stack where a fault cannot be handled.
+ *
+ * This only filters a block that is already unwritable when it is checked.
+ * The protection table is read without the virtual lock, because the thread
+ * may hold host locks that a virtual lock owner waits for (dlopen), so the
+ * pages can still be released, decommitted or reprotected before or while
+ * the block is written, and that write faults as before. Memory that Wine
+ * does not track counts as uncommitted. Write-watched pages count as
+ * writable and are handled by the existing write fault path.
+ * Returns FALSE without writing anything when the block is skipped.
+ */
+BOOL virtual_set_async_iosb( client_ptr_t iosb, NTSTATUS status, ULONG_PTR info )
+{
+    char *ptr = wine_server_get_ptr( iosb );
+    SIZE_T size = in_wow64_call() ? sizeof(IO_STATUS_BLOCK32) : sizeof(IO_STATUS_BLOCK);
+    char *page;
+
+    if (!iosb) return TRUE;
+    if ((UINT_PTR)ptr > ~(UINT_PTR)0 - size) return FALSE;
+
+    for (page = ROUND_ADDR( ptr, page_mask ); page < ptr + size; page += page_mask + 1)
+        if (!(get_unix_prot( get_page_vprot( page ) & ~VPROT_WRITEWATCH ) & PROT_WRITE)) return FALSE;
+
+    set_async_iosb( iosb, status, info );
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           virtual_set_force_exec
  *
